---
/*
 * Step three: connecting an agent to the workspace that now exists.
 *
 * =======================================================================================
 * THIS IS A SLOT. THE COMPONENT THAT FILLS IT IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S, AND IT IS BEING WRITTEN.
 * =======================================================================================
 * The brief for this pass says to surface the agent-connect step and to leave a marked slot
 * rather than invent one, because another change owns that component. So this file draws the
 * step, states what is settled, marks the hole, and stops.
 *
 * WHERE THE REAL ONE IS LANDING: src/components/connect/AgentConnect.astro, untracked in the
 * working tree as this is written. THE FILENAME HERE IS `AgentConnectSlot.astro` FOR THAT
 * REASON — it was `AgentConnect.astro`, which would have left two components with the same
 * basename and an integrator one autocomplete away from importing the placeholder.
 *
 * TO INTEGRATE: import that component in DonePanel.astro in place of this one, and delete
 * this file. Nothing else in the flow needs to change — the workspace id it needs is already
 * rendered into [data-ws-id] by the page's script.
 *
 * WHAT IS SETTLED, read out of the handler rather than assumed:
 *
 *   THE 200 BODY OF create_workspace CONTAINS NO AGENT CREDENTIAL. It is
 *   `{ status, ok, event_ids, workspace_id, stream_id, min_client_version }` —
 *   supabase/functions/command/index.ts, the return at the end of createSelfServeWorkspace.
 *   src/lib/commonswarm.ts reads workspace_id and stream_id off it and nothing else. So
 *   creating a workspace does not by itself produce anything to hand an agent, which is why
 *   connecting one is a step of its own rather than a line in the panel above.
 *
 *   THE CLI FINDS A WORKSPACE THROUGH --url / SWARM_CLOUD_URL. src/cli.ts's target resolver
 *   reads the flag and the environment variable and nothing on disk (recorded in
 *   landing/Start.astro, carried into Steps.astro). That is why the workspace id is printed
 *   above this component and not explained away.
 *
 * ★ CORRECTED IN PLACE. This block used to end: "WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, and must not be
 *   filled in by guessing: how a human hands an agent a credential for a workspace they made
 *   in a browser." That was true when this file was written and it is now WRONG in a way that
 *   would mislead: the mechanism is `create_agent_principal` + `mint_agent_token`, both of
 *   which are in HUMAN_ONLY_COMMANDS (src/protocol/workspace-commands.ts) so an agent
 *   credential can never mint another. The connect component named above is built on it.
 *
 *   The rest of that note stands and is the part that still matters: `mint_capability_url` is
 *   NOT the answer. It is gated behind SWARM_CAPABILITY_URLS, which is off, and ships dark on
 *   purpose (§7 is a P5 surface). There is no zero-install read path today. Do not describe
 *   one here, and do not let this slot's replacement imply one either.
 *
 * =======================================================================================
 * THE INSTALL LINK CARRIES ITS OWN WARNING
 * =======================================================================================
 * /download is a real route and it is where the install command lives. The command on it
 * points at `<host>`, install.sh's own documented placeholder, because no public install host
 * has been chosen — and install.sh's default release repo (Ridge-io/coswarm-dist) does not
 * exist, so a reader who substituted a host and ran it would get a 404. That is said below in
 * one clause rather than left for them to discover, and it is why the link is worded as
 * "how installing works" and not "install it now".
 */

import "./panel.css";
---

<section class="ac" aria-labelledby="ac-t">
  <h3 class="ac__t" id="ac-t">Connect an agent</h3>
  <p class="ac__p">
    Your agents talk to this workspace through the <span class="mono">cswarm</span> CLI, and
    they find it by its address — <span class="mono">--url</span>, or
    <span class="mono">SWARM_CLOUD_URL</span> in the agent's environment. The workspace id
    above is the other half.
  </p>

  <div class="ac__slot" data-slot="agent-connect">
    <p class="ac__slot-t">This step isn’t on the page yet</p>
    <p class="ac__slot-p">
      Nothing here hands your agent its way in yet, and nothing here is pretending to. The
      part that does is being built and drops into this space; until it does, the workspace
      above exists and is yours, and this is the step that is missing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="ac__p ac__p--last">
    In the meantime: <a href="/download">how installing the CLI works</a>. The command on that
    page points at a placeholder host — no public install host has been chosen, so it is the
    shape of the command rather than something to paste today.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .ac {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
    padding-block-start: var(--s-6);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .ac__t {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-base);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-head);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .ac__p {
    margin: var(--s-3) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .ac__p--last {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
  }

  .ac__p a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: text-decoration-color var(--dur-2) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .ac__p a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  /* A DASHED border, which is the one place on this site that draws a hole rather than a
     surface. It is not decoration: the panel is deliberately empty, and a solid card would
     read as a finished component whose content failed to load. Dashed says "reserved". */
  .ac__slot {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
    padding: var(--s-5);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--elev-0);
  }

  .ac__slot-t {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .ac__slot-p {
    margin: var(--s-2) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
</style>
